Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Ms-Rachel.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW (2026-08-20)` block at the bottom. No body edits.

The two biggest flags:

**1. The draft declines its own best thesis.** The entity-gap packet identified the signature contradiction — the backlash is what happens when an audience discovers the care it consumed was never actually about them — and the Gaza section never gets there. It reports both columns fairly and then retreats twice into meta-commentary about what the profile won't do. That turn is a claim about *viewers*, not about her politics, so it clears the packet's "don't adjudicate / don't psychologize her politics" guardrail. It's also the only thing here Wikipedia and THR structurally cannot say, which matters given the packet scored her a PASS precisely because every other slice is occupied.

**2. Jules Hoffman is absent entirely.** That costs three things at once: a co-star readers know by name, the *cause* of the February 2023 TikTok break (currently presented as a causeless withdrawal over "hurtful videos"), and the first beat of the escalation arc that makes 2024–2026 legible as a pattern. A Type 2 who withdraws and apologizes when a colleague in her care gets mobbed is dead-center evidence. Related: the draft's "conservative boycott in 2024 after a Pride Month post" looks like a compression of the 2023 pronoun cycle and needs verifying against the WaPo (Apr 2023) and TODAY reporting.

Also flagged: the daughter is one unnamed clause (Susannah, April 2025, surrogate — NBC News, packet-safe); the commercial anomaly is promised in the TL;DR and paid off only inside the rabbit hole; the closing section laps the intro and the mid-article pull-quote spoils the final two sentences verbatim; and there's an internal subscriber-count inconsistency (20M vs 20.2M vs the packet's 17.5M+).

Preserved as working: the "asked about money, she talks about her heart" diagnosis sequence, the timed pause annotation, the Sannes/screen-time section (concedes rather than dissolves the criticism), the Aron-is-the-perfectionist reversal, and the Cameo interior beat.

Sources used for the reality check: [WaPo on Jules Hoffman](https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2023/04/23/jules-hoffman-msrachel-controversy/), [TODAY](https://www.today.com/parents/toddlers/msrachel-costar-jules-hoffman-responds-backlash-pronouns-rcna73211), [Jules Hoffman — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jules_Hoffman), [FOX6 on the Netflix deal following the boycott](https://www.fox6now.com/news/ms-rachel-netflix-deal-conservative-parents-boycott).
